    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1177">

                <pb facs="1013" n="909" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg909"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/94.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consular Agent to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Worth</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 26, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Villa received me very cordially and signified his intention of extending
                    leniency to Spaniards in future. He is now operating against Federals towards
                    Ojinaga and Torreón. While I was there a very important conference was held
                    between Villa and two Carranza emissaries which was communicated to me. Villa
                    will be in Juárez on twenty-eighth.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. C. Carothers</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
